2
00:00:16,216 --> 00:00:20,604
[TH] Maria: 
I grew up in a fishing town much like this one,

3
00:00:20,628 --> 00:00:25,516
[TH] in a small South American country
you probably never heard of...

4
00:00:25,543 --> 00:00:30,832
[TH] But that village is long
gone, after a battle between

5
00:00:30,856 --> 00:00:35,743
[TH] U.C.S.-friendly government
forces and guerrillas.

6
00:00:42,826 --> 00:00:47,050
[TH] They destroyed everything...
My home, my family, everything I knew.

7
00:00:47,548 --> 00:00:51,560
[TH] The guerrillas were the ones
who took me under their wing.

8
00:00:51,952 --> 00:00:56,052
[TH] By the time I was fifteen, I
was fighting alongside them.

9
00:00:56,673 --> 00:01:01,673
[TH] I fought the U.C.S. and their
cronies with all the rage I could muster.

10
00:01:02,079 --> 00:01:04,645
[TH] That was all I had left, and all I knew.

11
00:01:04,664 --> 00:01:06,664
[TH] In the end, we were crushed...

12
00:01:06,900 --> 00:01:11,828
[TH] We were just a bunch of militants from
a backwards country it was inevitable.

13
00:01:11,889 --> 00:01:19,501
[TH] The few of us that were left were captured
and sent back to the mainland for trial.

14
00:01:26,420 --> 00:01:31,453
[TH] Maria:
And that's where he found me.

15
00:01:31,541 --> 00:01:35,581
[TH] \NM00:
...Driscoll.

16
00:01:36,063 --> 00:01:40,323
[TH] Maria: 
Yes. He promised to save me from execution

17
00:01:40,347 --> 00:01:43,023
[TH] if I agreed to work for him, as an agent.

18
00:01:43,320 --> 00:01:47,288
[TH] If I had known...I would've
just spat in his face and laughed.

19
00:01:47,908 --> 00:01:51,672
[TH] Driscoll wasn't even working
for the U.C.S. Day in and day out,

20
00:01:51,696 --> 00:01:56,260
[TH] I lied, killed, and betrayed
those who would trust us.

21
00:01:56,383 --> 00:02:00,083
[TH] All this for a goal that
only Driscoll knew.

22
00:02:00,187 --> 00:02:05,143
[TH] He's the one who put me in
the Black Hounds, you know?

23
00:02:05,993 --> 00:02:13,441
[TH] Maria: 
I've been betraying you since the first day we met.

24
00:02:13,517 --> 00:02:16,384
[TH] \NM00:
It doesn't matter now.

25
00:02:16,603 --> 00:02:24,523
[TH] I can't pretend to understand what you've
gone through, or what you had to do...

26
00:02:25,245 --> 00:02:29,213
[TH] \NM00:
But if you'll let me, I'll carry those burdens with you.

27
00:02:29,350 --> 00:02:33,683
[TH] As long as I can be with you.

28
00:02:34,671 --> 00:02:38,487
[TH] \NM00:
When I heard that you were still alive,

29
00:02:38,711 --> 00:02:46,147
[TH] that's all I could think about
being with you, no matter what.

30
00:02:46,383 --> 00:02:48,503
[TH] Maria:
Maybe...

31
00:02:48,518 --> 00:02:52,230
[TH] Maybe I was waiting for
someone to tell me that all along.

32
00:02:52,606 --> 00:02:55,406
[TH] You haven't changed, \NM00.

33
00:02:55,575 --> 00:02:59,415
[TH] Even being beaten and battered
by the war didn't change you.

34
00:02:59,963 --> 00:03:05,330
[TH] Maybe you're the
stronger of the two of us.

35
00:03:05,485 --> 00:03:10,785
[TH] Maria:
Me, I'm just...I'm just so tired.

36
00:03:10,941 --> 00:03:13,641
[TH] \NM00:
Rest if you're tired.

37
00:03:13,727 --> 00:03:16,507
[TH] Repent if you've sinned.

38
00:03:16,779 --> 00:03:19,559
[TH] Life lets us do that.

39
00:03:19,798 --> 00:03:23,378
[TH] We can always start over.
